---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/site/DocumentLayout.astro';
import Contact from '../components/site/Contact.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---

<DocumentLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="How SalahSide membership, app focus, and your choices work."
  legal
>
  <h2>App license</h2>
  <p>
    SalahSide is licensed through the App Store under <a
      href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/"
      >Apple's Standard End User License Agreement</a
    >. This page explains the product and membership. It does not replace that agreement or limit
    rights you have under applicable consumer law.
  </p>
  <h2>Membership and payment</h2>
  <p>
    Set up your prayer and optional focus preferences before choosing membership. SalahSide requires
    an active paid subscription or eligible introductory trial for membership features. Monthly and
    yearly plans are purchased through your Apple account; the localized price, billing period, and
    renewal terms appear in the app and Apple's purchase confirmation before you commit.
  </p>
  <p>
    A three-day free trial is available only when Apple confirms that your account and selected
    product are eligible for that offer. If you accept it, the subscription converts to the selected
    paid plan unless you cancel in time. A trial is not guaranteed for every account or storefront.
  </p>
  <h2>Renewal, cancellation, and restoration</h2>
  <p>
    Subscriptions renew automatically unless canceled through Apple. To manage or cancel, open
    iPhone Settings, tap your name, then Subscriptions, and select SalahSide. Follow the renewal or
    trial deadline shown by Apple; Apple recommends canceling a free or discounted trial at least 24
    hours before it ends.
  </p>
  <p>
    Deleting the app or using Erase local data does not cancel your subscription. To restore an
    existing purchase, use Restore purchases in SalahSide with the same Apple account. Access
    depends on a verified active entitlement. Pending or unverified purchases do not unlock
    membership.
  </p>
  <p>
    Apple handles billing and refund decisions. See <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/118428"
      >Apple's cancellation guide</a
    > or <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/118223">Apple's refund guide</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>Prayer times and check-ins</h2>
  <p>
    The first release supports London, New York, Toronto, Dubai, and Kuala Lumpur. Times depend on
    the city, its time zone, calculation method, Asr convention, high-latitude setting, and manual
    adjustments you choose. Compare these settings with your local mosque's timetable, including
    seasonal and Ramadan conventions. SalahSide is a personal aid and does not replace qualified
    religious guidance.
  </p>
  <p>
    Prayer check-ins are voluntary self-reports. SalahSide does not automatically mark a past prayer
    as completed or verify that you prayed.
  </p>
  <h2>Optional app focus and reminders</h2>
  <p>
    App focus needs Apple Screen Time permission and your selection of apps, categories, or
    websites. You can unlock the current prayer, change focus settings, or pause for one hour. These
    features depend on iOS permission and scheduling behavior. Keep access to essential apps in mind
    when selecting what to quiet.
  </p>
  <p>
    Reminders need notification permission and may be affected by iOS Focus, notification settings,
    or device state. Do not rely on app notifications or focus scheduling as your only timekeeping
    method.
  </p>
  <h2>Privacy and local data</h2>
  <p>
    Your settings and check-ins are stored on your device. Device backups may include them. Erase
    local data clears the app's settings, selections, and check-ins and releases its focus
    restrictions, but does not remove an Apple subscription or existing backups. Read the <a
      href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a
    > for details.
  </p>
  <h2>Support and updates</h2>
  <p>
    For product questions, visit <a href="/support/">Support</a> or contact <Contact />. Features
    and supported systems may change with updates. Changes to this page will show a new effective
    date.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
